# TeamPit — working rules for AI agents (Cursor & others)

Admin back-office for a **Shopee Thailand** car-A/C-parts shop (Den Air Service, Surin). Non-developer
owner, Thai/English — UI must be plain and scannable. Monorepo on the **Cloudflare** platform.

**Read these first (source-of-truth chain):**
1. [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) — the full project rules (TDD, Cloudflare, Shopee, GitHub).
2. [`docs/STATE_OF_THE_BUILD.md`](../../docs/STATE_OF_THE_BUILD.md) — the current as-built snapshot
   (what's done / in progress / next). **When a doc disagrees with the code, the code + this file win.**
3. [`docs/DECISIONS.md`](../../docs/DECISIONS.md) — confirmed product choices.
4. [`docs/API_REFERENCE.md`](../../docs/API_REFERENCE.md) · [`docs/SCHEMA_AS_BUILT.md`](../../docs/SCHEMA_AS_BUILT.md).

## Layout
- `apps/api` — Cloudflare Worker (`api.homeseeker.me`), **raw SQL over D1**, `StockLedger` Durable
  Object, R2 (`IMAGES`) + KV. Main file: `apps/api/src/index.ts`. Config: root `wrangler.jsonc`.
- `apps/mobile` — the Expo back office (TeamPit), published as a static website at teampit.formulal.cc (since 19–20 Nov 2026; admin.airplusauto.com only forwards: a phone opening it goes to the same page on teampit.formulal.cc, once it holds no unsent bill).
- `apps/storefront` — AirPlus, Next.js on OpenNext. (The old Next.js back office `apps/admin` was removed on
  18 Nov 2026; it lives on only in the git tag `old-back-office-final`.)
- `packages/core` — pure-TS money/sync logic (no I/O). `packages/db` — D1 SQL migrations only (no TS; nothing imports it).

## Must-not-break conventions
- **Money is integer satang** in D1 (1 THB = 100 satang); convert at the persistence boundary
  (`Math.round(thb*100)`). `packages/core` computes in THB decimals. Rates → basis points (7% → `700`).
- **TDD for money/stock/sync logic** — write the failing test first; show red→green. These are critical-path.
- Stock mutations go through the **`StockLedger` Durable Object** (single writer); `/sync` is **idempotent
  on `clientUuid`** and must never lose or double-count a sale or stock movement.
- Schema lives in **one place**: `packages/db/migrations/*.sql` (the applied DDL). There is no
  `schema.ts`. Keep migrations additive/nullable for safe rollout.
- Shop settings (incl. the bilingual shop info) live in **KV**, not D1 — no migration needed to add fields.

## The gate (run before claiming done)
```bash
npm run format && npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm test
```

## Agent gotchas (save yourself time)
- **Deploy is automatic:** pushing to `main` runs GitHub Actions which deploys the API, the AirPlus storefront and the back office app
  (secrets are set). No manual `npm run deploy` needed.
- **One CI check fails on every push and it's NOT your code:** `Workers Builds: kira-office` (Cloudflare's
  redundant Git integration) — its managed token lacks zone DNS edit for the custom domain. GitHub Actions
  already deploys. Ignore it / it should be disconnected in the Cloudflare dashboard. Never chase it as a bug.
- **Non-submit `<button>` needs `type="button"`** — inside a form a bare button submits on click.
- Live prod keeps intentional demo rows (`prod-demo`, 5 × `DEMO-AC-*`) — don't delete them as junk.

## GitHub
- Public repo `ladykirsah/TeamPit` (owner's choice, 18 Nov 2026) — never commit secrets or customer data. Don't force-push or rewrite history. Work on a branch and open a PR.
